# Super Kalooki design system

Source of truth: `../design-system/` (shared with the app, one level up in SuperKalooki/) (exported from the Design System artifact).

- Start with `../design-system/README.md` (rules, tokens, screen tiers, "Using this system in code").
- Tokens: use `../design-system/tokens.css` variables. Never hard-code hex, radius, shadow or font values.
- Components: each `../design-system/components/<Comp>/README.md` is the spec; `preview.html` is the visual reference. Rebuild components cleanly from spec + tokens — `components/bundle.css` is preview reference CSS, not a stylesheet to import wholesale.
- Never ship preview-only classes: `ct-`, `tm-`, `tl-`, `da-`, `ab-`, `mx-`.
- Screen tiers are the only breakpoints: `tier-short` (landscape ≤340px tall), `tier-phone` (landscape ≤430px tall), `tier-tablet` (landscape ≥981px wide). Website is portrait-first with `web-container`.
- Font: Inter only (800 headings, −0.02em). One gold (`--gold`); gold = commit, glass = cancel/tool, red = destroy. Move colours (blue Call, amber Lay, green Tack) only in the table dock.
- Mobile-first: landscape 780×360 is the design floor, 640×360 the minimum; 44px minimum touch targets.
- Table (app): follow `components/TableLayout/README.md` — hand fits without scrolling (44→24px step, 21px on tier-short), slide-to-select, lifted cards keep stack order, meld window fixed on the right and scrolls, +N opens a meld in place.
